@host = http://localhost:5283
# Dev placeholder values from the B2 setup (see docs/BackendSteps.md); change them if you changed your User Secrets.
@joinCode = DEV-2026
@adminName = Dev Admin
@adminPin = 1234

# Each request below is independent. In VS / VS Code the cookie jar is shared, so after a successful
# register or sign-in the later requests (me, sign-out) are authenticated as that player.

### OpenAPI document (Development only)
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

### Active event (public): name, year, themeKey
GET {{host}}/api/event

### Teams for the register screen (public). Expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/event/teams?code={{joinCode}}

### Wrong join code. Expect 404
GET {{host}}/api/event/teams?code=WRONG

### Register OK. Expect 201 + Set-Cookie + the me body
POST {{host}}/api/session/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "{{joinCode}}", "realName": "Alice Smith", "displayName": "Ally", "pin": "4321", "teamId": 1 }

### Register again with the same real name (any case/spacing). Expect 409 "Sign in instead"
POST {{host}}/api/session/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "{{joinCode}}", "realName": "  alice SMITH ", "displayName": "Other One", "pin": "4321", "teamId": 1 }

### Register with a taken display name. Expect 409 "Pick a different one"
POST {{host}}/api/session/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "{{joinCode}}", "realName": "Bob Jones", "displayName": "ALLY", "pin": "4321", "teamId": 1 }

### Register with invalid input (short name, empty display name, non-digit PIN). Expect 400 listing every field
POST {{host}}/api/session/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "{{joinCode}}", "realName": "A", "displayName": "", "pin": "12a4", "teamId": 1 }

### Register with a bad join code. Expect 404
POST {{host}}/api/session/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "WRONG", "realName": "Carol Jones", "displayName": "Caz", "pin": "4321", "teamId": 1 }

### Register with a team that doesn't exist in the event. Expect 400 (teamId)
POST {{host}}/api/session/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "{{joinCode}}", "realName": "Carol Jones", "displayName": "Caz", "pin": "4321", "teamId": 9999 }

### Sign in OK (case-insensitive name). Expect 200 + Set-Cookie
POST {{host}}/api/session/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "{{joinCode}}", "realName": "alice smith", "pin": "4321" }

### Sign in as the seeded admin. Expect 200, role "admin", no team
POST {{host}}/api/session/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "{{joinCode}}", "realName": "{{adminName}}", "pin": "{{adminPin}}" }

### Wrong PIN. Expect 401 "Real name or PIN is incorrect."
POST {{host}}/api/session/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "{{joinCode}}", "realName": "Alice Smith", "pin": "0000" }

### Unknown name. Expect the SAME 401 as the wrong PIN above
POST {{host}}/api/session/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "{{joinCode}}", "realName": "Nobody Here", "pin": "0000" }

### Rate limit: send this 6 times within 5 minutes (a "wrong PIN" for one name).
### Attempts 1-5 return 401; the 6th returns 429 + Retry-After, even with the right PIN.
### Other names are unaffected. The counter resets after 5 minutes or an app restart.
POST {{host}}/api/session/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "{{joinCode}}", "realName": "Rate Limit Test", "pin": "0000" }

### Me (signed in). Expect 200 with the caller's own real name, team from the DB
GET {{host}}/api/session/me

### Sign out. Expect 204 and the cookie cleared
POST {{host}}/api/session/signout

### Me after sign-out. Expect 401 (not a redirect)
GET {{host}}/api/session/me

# ======================= B4: teams + players =======================
# The cookie jar is shared, so "sign in as X" changes who every later request acts as. Each section says who it expects.
# @playerId / @otherPlayerId are Alice's and another player's ids from the register requests above; adjust if yours differ
# (GET /api/players as admin lists them). Team ids 1-6 are the seeded teams if you started from a fresh database.
@playerId = 2
@otherPlayerId = 3

### ---- As a PLAYER: sign in as Alice (registered above) ----
POST {{host}}/api/session/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "{{joinCode}}", "realName": "alice smith", "pin": "4321" }

### Teams as a player. Expect 200, members have displayName; realName is null except on Alice's own row
GET {{host}}/api/teams

### Edit my own names. Expect 200 with the new display name
PATCH {{host}}/api/players/me
Content-Type: application/json

{ "displayName": "Ally Cat" }

### Edit nothing. Expect 400
PATCH {{host}}/api/players/me
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Take someone else's display name (use any existing one, any case). Expect 409
PATCH {{host}}/api/players/me
Content-Type: application/json

{ "displayName": "TEST BOSS" }

### Player on admin routes. Expect 403 for each of these seven
GET {{host}}/api/players

###
POST {{host}}/api/teams
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sneaky", "colorKey": "teal", "iconKey": "star" }

###
PATCH {{host}}/api/teams/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sneaky" }

###
DELETE {{host}}/api/teams/1

###
PATCH {{host}}/api/players/{{otherPlayerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "displayName": "Hacked" }

###
PATCH {{host}}/api/players/{{playerId}}/team
Content-Type: application/json

{ "teamId": 2 }

###
POST {{host}}/api/players/{{playerId}}/promote

### ---- As the ADMIN ----
POST {{host}}/api/session/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinCode": "{{joinCode}}", "realName": "{{adminName}}", "pin": "{{adminPin}}" }

### Teams as admin. Expect every member's realName filled in
GET {{host}}/api/teams

### All players with real names and roles
GET {{host}}/api/players

### Create a team. Expect 201 and it appears last in GET /api/teams
POST {{host}}/api/teams
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Tea Party", "colorKey": "teal", "iconKey": "star" }

### Same name again (any case). Expect 409
POST {{host}}/api/teams
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "tea party", "colorKey": "orange", "iconKey": "star" }

### Existing colour. Expect 409
POST {{host}}/api/teams
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Other Team", "colorKey": "red", "iconKey": "star" }

### Bad input (short name, upper-case colour, empty icon). Expect 400 listing all three
POST {{host}}/api/teams
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "A", "colorKey": "Teal", "iconKey": "" }

### Rename. Expect 200 (set the id to the new team's id from the create response)
PATCH {{host}}/api/teams/7
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Tea Time" }

### Rename to another team's name. Expect 409
PATCH {{host}}/api/teams/7
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "smurfs" }

### Delete a team that has players (team 1 has Alice). Expect 409
DELETE {{host}}/api/teams/1

### Delete the empty team you created. Expect 204; a second delete gives 404
DELETE {{host}}/api/teams/7

### Admin edits a player's names. Expect 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/players/{{playerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "displayName": "Alice Renamed" }

### Move a player to another team. Expect 200 and the new team in GET /api/teams
PATCH {{host}}/api/players/{{playerId}}/team
Content-Type: application/json

{ "teamId": 2 }

### Move to a team that doesn't exist. Expect 400 (teamId)
PATCH {{host}}/api/players/{{playerId}}/team
Content-Type: application/json

{ "teamId": 9999 }

### Put an admin on a team (the seeded admin is usually player 1). Expect 400
PATCH {{host}}/api/players/1/team
Content-Type: application/json

{ "teamId": 2 }

### Promote a player. Expect 200, role "admin", no team; they leave their team's member list.
### Their old cookie still says Player until they sign in again (known limit).
POST {{host}}/api/players/{{otherPlayerId}}/promote

### Unknown player. Expect 404
POST {{host}}/api/players/999999/promote

# ======================= B5: scores =======================
# Sign in as the admin first (the "Sign in as the seeded admin" request above). Team ids 1-6 are the seeded teams on a
# fresh database; @scoreTeamId / @scorePlayerId are a team and a player (role Player, not an admin) to score.
# @adjustmentId is an id from the create or history responses below: set it before the reverse requests.
@scoreTeamId = 1
@scorePlayerId = 2
@adjustmentId = 1

### Team leaderboard (any signed-in user). Every team, zero totals included, highest first; tied teams share a rank (100, 100, 90 -> 1, 1, 3)
GET {{host}}/api/scores/teams

### Player leaderboard (admin). Every player-role player, zeros included, no admins; total desc then display name
GET {{host}}/api/scores/players

### Add 5 x 3 = 15 points to a team. Expect 201; the team's total in GET /api/scores/teams goes up by 15
POST {{host}}/api/scores/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "target": "team", "targetId": {{scoreTeamId}}, "amount": 5, "multiplier": 3, "direction": "add", "reason": "Round one" }

### Remove 4 points from a player (multiplier defaults to 1). Expect 201 with amount -4; the player's team total does NOT change
POST {{host}}/api/scores/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "target": "player", "targetId": {{scorePlayerId}}, "amount": 4, "direction": "remove" }

### Invalid input (amount 0, multiplier 101, no direction). Expect 400 listing amount, multiplier and direction
POST {{host}}/api/scores/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "target": "team", "targetId": {{scoreTeamId}}, "amount": 0, "multiplier": 101 }

### A team that does not exist, or an admin as the player target. Expect 400 (targetId)
POST {{host}}/api/scores/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "target": "team", "targetId": 999999, "amount": 5, "direction": "add" }

### Recent ledger rows, newest first. take is clamped to 1-100 (default 20). Reversed rows have isReversed true
GET {{host}}/api/scores/adjustments?take=10

### Undo an adjustment. Expect 201: an equal-and-opposite row with reversesAdjustmentId, and the total goes back
POST {{host}}/api/scores/adjustments/{{adjustmentId}}/reverse

### Undo the same adjustment again. Expect 409
POST {{host}}/api/scores/adjustments/{{adjustmentId}}/reverse

### Undo the undo (first set @adjustmentId to the id of the reversal row above). Expect 400
POST {{host}}/api/scores/adjustments/{{adjustmentId}}/reverse

### Unknown adjustment. Expect 404
POST {{host}}/api/scores/adjustments/999999999/reverse

### As a PLAYER (sign in as Alice again first): the team leaderboard works, everything else is 403
GET {{host}}/api/scores/players
